      "textSnapshot": "Problem:\nThe semantic provider and type scanners contained seven wrong-answer defects:\nCompleteness assurance gap — repositories with \u003e25% of tracked files never parsed (due to size limits) reported \"ok\" instead of \"degraded\", silencing correctness gates.\nGraphQL operation parsing — parameters with nested braces ($f: Filter = {enabled: true}) were rejected, losing entire operations.\nGraphQL tag detection — template literal tags separated from backticks by whitespace were not recognized, losing shorthand operations.\nGraphQL field name contamination — template interpolations (${expr}) produced invalid field names ($, n) in the graph.\nGo interface call binding — methods with mismatched signatures (e.g., Run(string) error vs. Run() error) were treated as valid implementations, producing wrong CALLS edges.\nGo qualified receiver routing — receivers like foo.Communicator resolved by directory basename instead of import path, picking decoy same-named packages over the actual import.\nIgnore policy explosion — one unreadable nested .gitignore failed the entire repository walk; now excludes only that subtree with a warning.\nVendor negation scope — a single !package/ in vendor/.gitignore re-admitted the whole vendored tree instead of just that package.\nAmbiguous registration aliases — command handler names appearing in multiple packages/languages attached the alias to all of them; now attach only when unambiguous.\nSolution:\nAdded hardened parsers and relation builders:\nCompleteness level now checks parsed-file ratio ≥75% and degrades below that threshold, catching silently degraded corpora.\nGraphQL parameter regex widened to allow nested braces; tag detection scans backward through whitespace; root field scanner rejects $-prefixed and backslash-escaped names.\nGo interface implementation checker validates parameter and result type signatures match before accepting a method as satisfying an interface requirement.\nGo qualified receiver resolver consults the file's import table to bind qualifiers to import paths, with basename fallback only when imports are unavailable.\nFilesystem walk fallback excludes subtrees whose .gitignore is unreadable (size or permission) and reports the omission as W_WALK_UNREADABLE_IGNORE_POLICY; operation-wide rule allowance errors still abort.\nVendored path verdict now checks ReincludesPath for each path individually instead of ReincludesDescendant on its ancestor.\nRegistration alias attachment deferred to after parsing the full corpus; aliases attach only to symbols with unique short names.\nNo public API change. Schema contract stable; SCIP IDs unchanged.",
      "etag": "W/\"2026-09-04T05:38:28.332542Z\""
    }
  }
}
